---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import law from '../../generated/law.json';
import OnPage from '../../components/OnPage.astro';
---
<Base title="The objections" description="Fourteen objections to the draft, published at full strength, each with its design consequences.">
  <p class="eyebrow">Memorandum · the honesty surface</p>
  <h1>The objections, at full strength</h1>
  <p class="intro prose">
    Every serious argument against this Regulation, stated as well as its
    opponents would state it, before a single article was drafted. Each
    objection ends in design consequences, and the design-constraints
    table below is a merge criterion: text that violates it does not
    merge. Where an objection is conceded, it says so. This page is the
    campaign's credibility strategy, not its confession: read it first,
    then read <a href="/law">the law it produced</a>.
  </p>
  <div class="withtoc">
    <OnPage toc={law.objections.toc} />
    <div class="prose objections" set:html={law.objections.html} />
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  h1 { font-size: 1.7rem; margin: 0.4rem 0 1rem; }
  .intro { margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .objections :global(h2) { border-top: 1px solid var(--guilloche); padding-top: 1.4rem; }
</style>
